window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>\"Trust me to fall for someone who wasn't emotionally available.\" Jennifer's heart ached and started to crack. \"Touché, karma!\"</b></p> <p>Jennifer Gains is a successful editor at a prestigious New York publishing house who's dragged back to her bittersweet past by a new television series.</p> <p>Five years ago, Jennifer left behind Plum Island and the beloved aunt who raised her after her mother's untimely death. Coming back is bittersweet, but work calls, and she's caught up in helping her friend produce her new television series, Cobble Cottage Mysteries.</p> <p>Until she visits her Aunt Betty to find the Beach Plum Cottage in disrepair and her aunt gravely ill. Dedicated and practical as always, Jennifer immediately sets about fixing things. She doesn't want Aunt Betty to call upon the old island contractor, but when she sees a rugged man with piercing green eyes, her thoughts—and heart—flip on their head.</p> <p>Harley Donovan is the young, handsome nephew of the island's old contractor, and to Jennifer, he's an enigma. No one is this nice and helpful. Not genuinely. As she sets about trying to find Harley's dark side, sparks fly as their differences clash.</p> <p>Jennifer must confront her past, grapple with her aunt's failing health, and navigate the island's undeniable pull on her heart.</p> <p>The Cottage on Plum Island <i>weaves a tale of love, healing, and unexpected discoveries against the enchanting backdrop of Plum Island. It is book two of the Cobble Beach Romance Series, a powerful clean and wholesome women's saga in which heartwarming strong characters have a second chance at romance if they believe it is possible and let go of the past. This series is best enjoyed in order.</i></p>"; 
